<title>VENEZUELA: U.S. must expand Latin trade, George Bush says.</title>
<headline>U.S. must expand Latin trade, George Bush says.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS, Venezuela 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Former U.S. President George Bush reiterated Wednesday his vision of a hemispheric trade zone in the Americas and warned that the United States ignored its neighbors at its own peril.</p>
<p>Speaking as guest of honor at an international oil conference in Caracas, Bush slammed those opposed to the U.S. integration with Latin America.</p>
<p>&quot;The America-first approach is short-sighted and puts the U.S. last in terms of respect,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
